WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:08.582
"Oh no!"

2
00:00:13.705 --> 00:00:14.445
Zann exclaimed.

3
00:00:14.885 --> 00:00:15.846
He dropped the stone.

4
00:00:16.726 --> 00:00:19.307
Instantly the vision of his parents was gone.

5
00:00:19.327 --> 00:00:20.768
"What is it?"

6
00:00:20.968 --> 00:00:21.588
Perda asked.

7
00:00:21.608 --> 00:00:23.089
"Did you see them too?"

8
00:00:24.169 --> 00:00:26.730
Zann nodded, too overwhelmed to speak.

9
00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:30.852
His parents had looked so real—and so scared!

10
00:00:31.596 --> 00:00:33.517
"But why are we seeing them now?"

11
00:00:33.817 --> 00:00:34.437
Perda wondered.

12
00:00:34.457 --> 00:00:37.838
"I've touched that stone lots of times."

13
00:00:39.218 --> 00:00:42.639
"Message stones are mysterious things," Wyssa said.

14
00:00:42.659 --> 00:00:46.800
"They hold on to the magical essence of all who touch them."

15
00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:51.041
"That's how Mother used the stone to help us," Gliss put in.

16
00:00:51.061 --> 00:00:53.222
"Mother? Who's that?"

17
00:00:53.482 --> 00:00:54.102
Venna asked.

18
00:00:54.902 --> 00:01:00.524
Gliss, Perda, and Darb quickly told her about their adventure in Zon, the world with no boys.

19
00:01:02.008 --> 00:01:04.770
"Interesting," Wyssa said when they'd finished.

20
00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:12.836
"Mother's spell must have made the stone's messages stronger, allowing Perda to see them too."

21
00:01:13.957 --> 00:01:16.559
"Does this mean Zann's parents are nearby?"

22
00:01:16.779 --> 00:01:17.439
Gliss asked.

23
00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:18.940
Wyssa nodded.

24
00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:23.784
"Such magic works best when it's close to the source of the message."

25
00:01:23.804 --> 00:01:27.286
"The source—you mean Zann's parents?"

26
00:01:27.546 --> 00:01:28.147
Darb asked.

27
00:01:28.167 --> 00:01:30.372
"Are they here in Rood?"

28
00:01:30.392 --> 00:01:32.653
"It seems likely," said Wyssa.

29
00:01:33.513 --> 00:01:34.333
Zann gasped.

30
00:01:34.353 --> 00:01:36.674
"Oh!" Wyssa continued.

31
00:01:36.694 --> 00:01:43.776
"My guess is that Morb has just returned to wherever he's holding Zann's parents captive, and they became

32
00:01:43.916 --> 00:01:50.417
frightened." "And their fear caused the stone to send that vision to whoever was touching it."

33
00:01:50.778 --> 00:01:52.178
Venna peered at the stone.

34
00:01:52.198 --> 00:01:59.580
"Fascinating!" "If Morb is back with his prisoners, he probably found the Horn already," Perda pointed out.

35
00:02:00.452 --> 00:02:01.573
"Not necessarily."

36
00:02:01.873 --> 00:02:03.053
Wyssa turned to Venna.

37
00:02:03.073 --> 00:02:04.794
"Tell me where it is."

38
00:02:04.814 --> 00:02:08.536
"Wait!" Zann blurted out before Venna could respond.

39
00:02:08.556 --> 00:02:09.996
"Don't tell her."

40
00:02:10.016 --> 00:02:13.018
"What?" Wyssa glared at Zann.

41
00:02:13.038 --> 00:02:16.319
"This is no time for games, boy."

42
00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:22.922
Zann felt nervous, especially when he remembered how easily Wyssa had broken his Shackle spell.

43
00:02:23.262 --> 00:02:24.543
But he stood his ground.

44
00:02:24.563 --> 00:02:27.464
"I know you want to punish Morb," he said.

45
00:02:28.172 --> 00:02:30.374
"But first we need to find my parents.

46
00:02:31.294 --> 00:02:33.916
Morb might be the only one who can lead us to them."

47
00:02:34.837 --> 00:02:36.918
He expected Wyssa to get even angrier.

48
00:02:37.719 --> 00:02:40.220
Instead she looked at the ground and sighed.

49
00:02:41.481 --> 00:02:43.222
"You're right," she said.

50
00:02:43.242 --> 00:02:46.364
"This is my chance to make things right.

51
00:02:46.985 --> 00:02:53.129
Not just by making Morb pay for what he's done, but also by doing what I can to

52
00:02:53.189 --> 00:02:54.890
help Nax and Asta."

53
00:02:54.910 --> 00:02:57.552
"Thanks." Zann was relieved.

54
00:02:57.932 --> 00:03:00.073
He told Wyssa where they'd seen the Horn.

55
00:03:00.913 --> 00:03:02.273
Her expression darkened again.

56
00:03:02.293 --> 00:03:05.434
"The only thing hiding it was some rubble?

57
00:03:06.574 --> 00:03:10.195
I'm sure Morb had the Horn within seconds after leaving here."

58
00:03:11.316 --> 00:03:14.617
"We need to find him before he uses it," Venna said.

59
00:03:14.637 --> 00:03:15.817
"But how?

60
00:03:16.377 --> 00:03:19.158
I don't know if he has a lair here in Rood."

61
00:03:19.178 --> 00:03:21.118
"I have an idea."

62
00:03:21.519 --> 00:03:23.439
Wyssa pursed her lips and whistled.

63
00:03:24.139 --> 00:03:26.200
Several tiny people zapped into view.

64
00:03:26.728 --> 00:03:27.849
Whistlefeather was among them.

65
00:03:27.869 --> 00:03:29.471
"Have you found him?"

66
00:03:29.651 --> 00:03:31.132
Whistlefeather asked eagerly.

67
00:03:31.152 --> 00:03:32.493
"Is Morb gone?"

68
00:03:32.513 --> 00:03:35.356
"I'm afraid not," Wyssa said.

69
00:03:35.376 --> 00:03:36.677
"We need your help.

70
00:03:37.077 --> 00:03:39.219
Does he have a lair in this world?"

71
00:03:40.681 --> 00:03:43.903
Whistlefeather hesitated, trading a look with the other Roodians.

72
00:03:45.004 --> 00:03:48.688
"Yes, but His voice trailed off.

73
00:03:48.708 --> 00:03:53.372
"We'd like to help," a Roodian woman said, her voice trembling.

74
00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:56.681
"But we fear Morb's retribution.

75
00:03:57.361 --> 00:03:59.542
He's holding our queen prisoner."

76
00:03:59.562 --> 00:04:01.283
"Your queen?"

77
00:04:01.703 --> 00:04:04.644
Zann recalled the tiny, frightened woman from his vision.

78
00:04:05.705 --> 00:04:06.645
Whistlefeather nodded.

79
00:04:06.665 --> 00:04:11.707
"We're afraid that if we tell you where Morb's lair is, he'll toss the queen through the nearest

80
00:04:11.767 --> 00:04:13.948
wormhole." Perda shrugged.

81
00:04:14.248 --> 00:04:15.629
"What's so bad about that?"

82
00:04:15.649 --> 00:04:18.970
"It would kill her," Wyssa said grimly.

83
00:04:18.990 --> 00:04:23.572
"The Roodians told me they cannot pass through any wormhole."

84
00:04:24.428 --> 00:04:25.689
The Roodian woman nodded.

85
00:04:25.709 --> 00:04:28.030
"Many have tried in the past.

86
00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:31.931
All were flung back into Rood—lifeless."

87
00:04:31.951 --> 00:04:34.252
"Wow," Gliss said.

88
00:04:34.272 --> 00:04:37.914
"I guess that's why Rood stayed undiscovered for so long."

89
00:04:37.934 --> 00:04:42.836
"Well, it explains why Roodians can't visit other worlds."

90
00:04:43.897 --> 00:04:46.378
Perda glanced at a wormhole blinking nearby.

91
00:04:46.398 --> 00:04:50.860
"But there are wormholes to so many other worlds here!

92
00:04:51.860 --> 00:04:54.701
I'm surprised nobody has ever come through one of them."

93
00:04:54.721 --> 00:05:00.122
"The wormholes here don't work like most wormholes," Whistlefeather said.

94
00:05:00.142 --> 00:05:03.363
"One can pass from Rood to any other world.

95
00:05:03.943 --> 00:05:06.664
But the wormholes only work in one direction.

96
00:05:07.544 --> 00:05:10.245
Rood itself can only be reached via the vortex."

97
00:05:11.185 --> 00:05:12.666
"Yes," Wyssa added.

98
00:05:12.686 --> 00:05:16.267
"And there's only one incoming wormhole in Rood.

99
00:05:16.867 --> 00:05:18.327
It's very unpredictable."

100
00:05:19.307 --> 00:05:21.108
She sighed, rubbing her forehead.

101
00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:24.663
"In any case, we can't endanger the queen.

102
00:05:25.463 --> 00:05:29.267
We'll have to find another way "Wait."

103
00:05:29.647 --> 00:05:31.188
A young Roodian stepped forward.

104
00:05:31.969 --> 00:05:34.071
"Any other way will take too long.

105
00:05:34.691 --> 00:05:36.153
We'll tell you where Morb is."

106
00:05:37.294 --> 00:05:38.615
"Prince Doni, no!"

107
00:05:38.895 --> 00:05:40.056
another Roodian exclaimed.

108
00:05:40.656 --> 00:05:44.219
"Your mother—" "My mother would want us to help these people."

109
00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:47.002
The prince squared his tiny shoulders.

110
00:05:47.022 --> 00:05:49.184
"She's the bravest person I know.

111
00:05:50.232 --> 00:05:53.833
She would want to defeat Morb, no matter the risk to her own safety."

112
00:05:54.873 --> 00:05:55.874
He snapped his fingers.

113
00:05:56.374 --> 00:05:58.494
A piece of parchment appeared in his hand.

114
00:05:58.514 --> 00:06:04.536
"Morb is forcing many of our people to act as his servants, cleaning the lair and preparing food.

115
00:06:05.036 --> 00:06:06.237
They drew this map."

116
00:06:06.257 --> 00:06:09.037
"Why would Morb need servants?"

117
00:06:09.297 --> 00:06:09.918
Darb wondered.

118
00:06:09.938 --> 00:06:12.678
"He should be able to do that stuff with magic."

119
00:06:13.519 --> 00:06:16.439
"He loves bossing people around," said Perda.

120
00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:18.400
"That's probably why."

121
00:06:19.720 --> 00:06:21.161
Wyssa was examining the map.

122
00:06:21.181 --> 00:06:23.983
"Thank you," she told the Roodians.

123
00:06:24.003 --> 00:06:27.105
"We'll try to rescue your queen if we can."

124
00:06:27.926 --> 00:06:29.587
Prince Doni nodded his thanks.

125
00:06:29.607 --> 00:06:31.729
"But be careful!"

126
00:06:32.009 --> 00:06:32.469
he warned.

127
00:06:32.489 --> 00:06:35.311
"The Gray Gorge is a dangerous place."

128
00:06:36.492 --> 00:06:38.233
Zann wasn't worried about danger.

129
00:06:38.774 --> 00:06:40.215
He had to find his parents!

130
00:06:40.235 --> 00:06:42.216
"What are we waiting for?"

131
00:06:42.476 --> 00:06:42.817
he said.

132
00:06:42.837 --> 00:06:43.757
"Let's go!"

133
00:06:44.858 --> 00:06:45.559
Wyssa nodded.

134
00:06:48.704 --> 00:06:51.066
"Zap!" Zann landed with a grunt on hard ground.

135
00:06:51.826 --> 00:06:57.731
Looking up he saw a forbidding stone tower shrouded in ghostly gray fog.

136
00:06:58.572 --> 00:07:03.595
He looked down and realized everyone was standing near the edge of a huge chasm.

137
00:07:04.476 --> 00:07:07.238
It was so deep Zann couldn't see the bottom.

138
00:07:08.099 --> 00:07:12.602
A howling wind whipped in and out of it, pulling in anything it could grab.

139
00:07:13.483 --> 00:07:17.935
"Aah!" Zann cried as he felt himself suddenly losing balance.
